    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> be ten observation of a random variable <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>10</mn></munderover><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>10</mn></munderover><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math> where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8800;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>,&nbsp;then the standard deviation of these observations is:<br />&nbsp;",
